# .dockerignore — what NOT to send into the Docker build context.
#
# Goal: tighten the context to exactly what the Dockerfile needs (Go
# sources, web/ source, go.mod / go.sum) so each `docker build`:
#   1. Sends the daemon a smaller tarball → faster builds
#   2. Doesn't accidentally embed dev state (data/*.db, .env, *.log)
#      into a layer where it would persist for whoever pulls the image
#
# Critical embed boundaries (DO NOT exclude these via wildcards):
#   - internal/prompts/integration.md   (//go:embed integration.md)
#   - web/dist/**                       (//go:embed all:dist, but
#                                        regenerated by frontend stage —
#                                        safe to exclude from CONTEXT
#                                        because the backend stage gets
#                                        it via COPY --from=frontend)
#
# Maintenance rule: any file the Dockerfile COPYs MUST NOT match a
# pattern below. The Dockerfile copies:
#   - go.mod, go.sum                   (backend stage)
#   - everything via `COPY . .`        (backend stage — needs all .go
#                                      AND internal/prompts/*.md)
#   - web/package*.json, then web/     (frontend stage)
# Patterns below are anchored at the root with explicit paths rather
# than relying on `*.md` / `*.json` glob recursion, which silently
# matched embedded markdown the first time this file was written.

# ── VCS metadata ────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

# ── Build outputs (regenerated inside the image) ───────
bin/
/depsilo
web/dist/
web/node_modules/
web/.astro/
web/.vite/

# ── Runtime / dev state we must never ship ─────────────
data/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.log
.dev.log
.server.pid
config.toml
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Test infrastructure (not needed inside the image) ──
testground/
tests/

# ── Root-level docs (enumerated explicitly so subdirectory
#    *.md — including the embedded internal/prompts/integration.md
#    — stays in the build context) ───────────────────────
/CHANGELOG.md
/CLAUDE.md
/CONTEXT.md
/CONTRIBUTING.md
/DESIGN.md
/README.md
/README_zh.md
/RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md
/SECURITY.md
/docs/

# ── Packaging configs (irrelevant to the server image) ─
Formula/
assets/linux/
assets/macos/
scripts/build-macos-app.sh
scripts/install-linux.sh
scripts/i18n-audit.py
install.sh
.goreleaser.yaml

# ── Docker / compose (we're INSIDE the build — don't ship them) ─
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore

# ── IDE / editor / OS junk ─────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── SBOMs / signatures generated in CI ────────────────
dist/
*.cdx.json
*.spdx.json
*.sig
*.intoto.jsonl

# Note: LICENSE intentionally kept — OSS image consumers and some
# package registries expect it to land alongside the binary.
